From: Banana <bananalinux@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 28 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gfx/vulkan: turn the menu with the panel on KMS/GBM

SwanStation's Vulkan renderer runs on the RPC through Turnip (video_driver =
"vulkan" + khr_display), and vulkan_draw_blit_menu blits with mvp_menu, which
vulkan_set_projection left as trn x mvp_no_rot -- unrotated. Where a window system
owns the output's orientation that is fine (ROCKNIX runs RetroArch windowed under
sway, which turns the output, and carries no rotation patch), but on KMS/GBM there
is nothing above RetroArch, so on a panel mounted turned in the shell the game
comes out rotated by video_rotation and the menu stays in the framebuffer's
portrait orientation, reading sideways. The gl2 and gl3 drivers already turn their
menu (patches 0005/0008); this is the same for the Vulkan driver.

Build mvp_menu the way the driver builds the content's mvp -- trn x menu_rot x
mvp_no_rot -- with the menu rotation taken from the *user's* video_rotation (never
the core's, so a vertical arcade game cannot spin the interface), at this driver's
own 270-per-step angle (Vulkan's flipped Y), i.e. the same value vulkan_set_rotation
hands the content.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/gfx/drivers/vulkan.c
+++ b/gfx/drivers/vulkan.c
@@ -4023,8 +4023,31 @@
    }
    matrix_4x4_multiply(vk->mvp, trn, tmp);
 
-   /* Required for translate_x+y / negative offsets to also work in RGUI */
-   matrix_4x4_multiply(vk->mvp_menu, trn, vk->mvp_no_rot);
+   /* Required for translate_x+y / negative offsets to also work in RGUI. The menu is blitted with
+    * mvp_menu; where a window system owns the output's orientation leaving it unrotated is fine, but on
+    * KMS/GBM there is nothing above RetroArch, so on a panel mounted turned in the shell (the Retroid
+    * Pocket Classic's 1080x1240 in a landscape body) the game comes out rotated by video_rotation and
+    * the menu stays in the framebuffer's portrait orientation, reading sideways. Turn it with the user's
+    * video_rotation -- never the core's, so a vertical arcade game cannot spin the interface -- the same
+    * the gl2 and gl3 drivers already do, at this driver's own 270-per-step angle (Vulkan's flipped Y). */
+   {
+      settings_t *settings   = config_get_ptr();
+      unsigned user_rotation = settings ? (settings->uints.video_rotation % 4) : 0;
+      float menu_radians     = M_PI * (270.0f * user_rotation) / 180.0f;
+      float menu_cosine      = cosf(menu_radians);
+      float menu_sine        = sinf(menu_radians);
+      math_matrix_4x4 menu_rot, menu_tmp;
+
+      memset(&menu_rot, 0, sizeof(menu_rot));
+      MAT_ELEM_4X4(menu_rot, 0, 0) = menu_cosine;
+      MAT_ELEM_4X4(menu_rot, 0, 1) = -menu_sine;
+      MAT_ELEM_4X4(menu_rot, 1, 0) = menu_sine;
+      MAT_ELEM_4X4(menu_rot, 1, 1) = menu_cosine;
+      MAT_ELEM_4X4(menu_rot, 2, 2) = 1.0f;
+      MAT_ELEM_4X4(menu_rot, 3, 3) = 1.0f;
+      matrix_4x4_multiply(menu_tmp, menu_rot, vk->mvp_no_rot);
+      matrix_4x4_multiply(vk->mvp_menu, trn, menu_tmp);
+   }
 }
 
 static void vulkan_set_rotation(void *data, unsigned rotation)
